meta {
  name: transfer-provider
}

docs {
  DSP 2025-1 Transfer Process, HTTPS binding: the provider's endpoints, called as the
  consumer (the collection gets a DCP token for each request). These take DSP messages;
  the consumer's management API ("management/Start transfer") is another API.
  They need an agreement the consumer's DID holds, in the variable agreementId:
  - "two-connectors": run "management/Start negotiation" and "Get negotiation", which
    saves agreementId (the consumer connector and this collection share one DID);
  - "single": run "negotiation-provider" steps 1 to 3 with the fake consumer of
    docs/TESTING.md, then copy the agreement's @id from what the fake consumer printed
    into the environment variable agreementId.
  The provider calls back {{callbackAddress}}: keep the fake consumer (port 9000)
  running. It prints the TransferStartMessage with the data address.
}
